        "params": {
          "text": "**FN01 \u2014 One sample of memory**  \n**1 Predict \u2192 2 Run \u2192 3 Inspect \u2192 4 Change one thing.** Run **2 s at 10 Hz**, then open Scope.  \n`y[n]=u[n]+0.5 y[n\u22121]`; stored past `y[\u22121]=0 V`.  \nPredict output: 1, 1.5, 1.75, 1.875 V. The previous channel is one sample behind.  \nTry: select output_gain, press F4, change factor 0.5 to 1.25; rerun. Does it settle?  \n[Open FN01 student lab](qrc:/s7studio/help/education/labs/FN01-unit-delay/README.md) \u00b7 [MIT difference equations](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_chap1/) \u00b7 [MIT block diagrams](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/6-003-signals-and-systems-fall-2011/resources/mit6_003f11_chap3/)",
          "text_format": "markdown",
